.TH VSCHEDULER 1 "July 2025" "Pawsey Supercomputing Centre" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vscheduler \- Session Management and Reporting Platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vscheduler
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] <\fICOMMAND\fR> [\fISUBCOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Session Management and Reporting Platform for Pawsey Supercomputing Centre. Supports node status management and wall time exceptions.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B vset
Set node status.
.RS
.IP "\-status <STATUS>"
Required. New status for the node.
.RE

.TP
.B vexcept
Set wall time different to others.
.RS
.IP "\-mode <MODE>"
Required. New wall time mode.
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-u " USERNAME"
Optional. No username will run across all users.
.TP
.BI \-n " NODE"
Optional. No node name will run across all nodes.
.TP
.BI \-d " DATE"
Date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Having only one date will search from first DB record. No date will search across all records.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print detailed logs during processing.
.TP
.B --version
Show program's version number and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show this help message and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B vscheduler vset -status up -n node01 --verbose
Set node01 status to "up" with verbose output.
.TP
.B vscheduler vexcept -mode activate -u alice -d 2025-07-01 2025-07-14
Activate wall time exception for user alice between specified dates.

.SH AUTHOR
Pawsey Supercomputing Centre

